From 4f867d37fe6425b665c06c40168920cf6d6d684a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The transcript autolink's start search stops 1,024 characters
 into the rest of a paragraph and cuts the text before a whitespace run
 instead of scanning the whole remainder on every inline step, so lexing a 131
 KB single-paragraph reply (the benchmark's long rows) scans about 1 MB
 instead of 71 MB and takes about 6 ms instead of 55 ms in V8, with tokens
 identical to the unbounded search for links, emails and hard breaks at and
 past the cut.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QtZVtcNTgBwKhSN8i2v1w2
---
 .../ui/src/context/marked-autolink.test.ts    | 36 ++++++++++++++++++-
 packages/ui/src/context/marked.tsx            | 32 +++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/ui/src/context/marked-autolink.test.ts b/packages/ui/src/context/marked-autolink.test.ts
index 8460b5b7..bde351b9 100644
